{number: 162}
{title: And Can It Be?}
{key: C}

{start_of_verse: 1}
And [C] can it be that [F] I should [C] gain
An interest in the [G7] Savior's [C] blood?
Died He for me, who [F] caused His [C] pain?
For me, who Him to [G7] death pur-[C] sued?
A-[G] mazing [C] love! how [F] can it [C] be
That Thou, my [F] God, shouldst [C] die [G7] for [C] me?
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 2}
'Tis [C] myst'ry all! The Im-[F] mortal [C] dies:
Who can explore His [G7] strange de-[C] sign?
In vain the firstborn [F] seraph [C] tries
To sound the depths of [G7] love di-[C] vine.
'Tis [G] mercy [C] all! Let [F] earth a-[C] dore,
Let angel [F] minds in-[C] quire [G7] no [C] more.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
He [C] left His Father's [F] throne a-[C] bove—
So free, so infinite [G7] His [C] grace!
Emptied Himself of [F] all but [C] love,
And bled for Adam's [G7] helpless [C] race.
'Tis [G] mercy [C] all, im-[F] mense and [C] free;
For, O my [F] God, it [C] found [G7] out [C] me.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 4}
Long [C] my imprisoned [F] spirit [C] lay
Fast bound in sin and [G7] nature's [C] night;
Thine eye diffused a [F] quick'ning [C] ray,
I woke, the dungeon [G7] flamed with [C] light;
My [G] chains fell [C] off, my [F] heart was [C] free,
I rose, went [F] forth, and [C] fol-[G7] lowed [C] Thee.
{end_of_verse}
